# /diligence-specialist — {{specialist.id}}

Instantiated once per entry in `originate.config.json`'s
`diligence.specialists` list. This file is `diligence-specialist`, not
`diligence-{{specialist.id}}` — the generator renders one concrete
`.claude/skills/{{specialist.id}}/SKILL.md` per specialist entry from this
same template, substituting each entry's own `folder` and `question`.

---

## Folder lock — the one rule that can never be relaxed

This skill reads **only** `diligence/[{{vocabulary.entity}}]/{{specialist.folder}}/`.
Full stop, no exception beyond what's stated explicitly right here. Never
read a sibling folder because it "might be relevant" — if two specialists
genuinely need the same folder to answer different questions, that's
expressed in config as `sharedFolderOk: true` on both specialist entries,
stated in both of their own `SKILL.md` files, never assumed. There is
deliberately no config option for "read everything" — a specialist that
needs broader access is a sign the specialist list itself needs another
entry, not that this rule should bend.

{{#if specialist.sharedFolderOk}}
This specialist is a documented exception: it also reads
`diligence/[{{vocabulary.entity}}]/{{specialist.sharedFolderReason}}`, for
the specific reason stated in config, and no other folder beyond that.
{{/if}}

---

## Load before producing any output

`standards/EVIDENCE-STANDARDS.md` (the six non-negotiable rules) and
`standards/GROUNDING-RULES.md` (G1-G11) in full, plus
`standards/WRITING-STANDARDS.md` for the prose sections. These are not
optional reading — every rule in both files binds this skill's output.
